# Runtime Debug Discipline

When debugging:
- capture the Request ID for Cursor or MCP failures
- use DevTools console only when the failure looks Cursor-level
- separate repo/runtime bugs from MCP-routing bugs and sandbox policy issues
- prefer the smallest reproducible case before changing code

Failure classes to distinguish:
- repo code or configuration
- MCP connection, routing, or server behavior
- sandbox or network policy
- Cursor product behavior

Do not start patching until the failure class is explicit.
